<concept base="Anywhere" id="t00463">
	<title>Emergency Braking</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e03176">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e03177">
								<image href="images/N_SP3i25_C00_011_IR.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e03178">
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Emergency Braking</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>Emergency Braking can alert you with Forward Safety warning light blinking (<image href="images/WKIA_037.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/>), a warning message, an audible warning and steering wheel vibration (if equipped).</p>
		<p>Emergency Braking may be activated in the following conditions:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<p>Your driving speed is approximately 30-130 km/h (19-80 mph).</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>The oncoming vehicle speed is above approximately 10 km/h (6 mph).</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>A target enters the operating range of the Direct Oncoming function.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</conbody>
	<related-links>
